---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Studio BDY"
  description="Studio BDY provides programme and delivery management to directors who need an experienced hand, and practical help for small businesses adopting AI, automating spreadsheets and building bespoke apps. Based in Bath, working remotely with clients in the UK and internationally."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container stack gap-m">
      <p class="eyebrow">Programme &amp; delivery management · Bath, UK · Remote worldwide</p>
      <h1 style="max-width: 900px">Delivery support for programmes that have to land.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Studio BDY provides programme and delivery management to directors who need an experienced hand, and practical help for small businesses adopting AI, automating spreadsheets and building bespoke apps.</p>
      <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top: 12px">
        <a href="mailto:lee@studiobdy.com" class="btn btn-primary">Talk to Lee</a>
        <a href="#services" class="btn btn-secondary">See services</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="proof">
        <div>
          <strong>Telecoms · Pharma · Public sector</strong>
          <p>Programme delivery in regulated, complex environments.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>Many industries, several countries</strong>
          <p>Freelance Excel and small-business work, delivered remotely.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>People in the loop</strong>
          <p>AI and automation that assists, with a person approving what matters.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="services" class="section surface">
    <div class="container stack gap-l">
      <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px">
        <div class="stack gap-s">
          <p class="eyebrow">Services</p>
          <h2>What Studio BDY does</h2>
        </div>
        <a href="/services/" style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; text-decoration: none">All services →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <p class="num">01</p>
          <h3>Programme management &amp; governance</h3>
          <p>Running programmes end to end: planning, governance, risk, business engagement, stakeholder and customer management, RFP support, and the day-to-day drive that gets teams delivering results.</p>
          <a class="more" href="/services/#programme">Programme delivery →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="num">02</p>
          <h3>AI for small businesses</h3>
          <p>Practical help adopting AI into day-to-day work: finding the tasks worth handing over, setting it up safely, and keeping a person in the loop.</p>
          <a class="more" href="#example">See an example →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="num">03</p>
          <h3>Excel solutions &amp; automation</h3>
          <p>Spreadsheets that do the work: models, reporting and automation built to be maintained by your team, not just delivered.</p>
          <a class="more" href="/services/#excel">Excel &amp; automation →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="num">04</p>
          <h3>Bespoke mobile apps</h3>
          <p>iPhone and iPad apps built for one specific job, for when off-the-shelf software doesn't fit the way you work.</p>
          <a class="more" href="/services/#apps">Mobile apps →</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="example" class="section band">
    <div class="container stack gap-xl">
      <div class="two-col" style="align-items: center">
        <div class="stack gap-m">
          <p class="eyebrow">AI in the day-to-day</p>
          <h2>An inbox that watches for the emails that matter</h2>
          <p style="font-size: 17px">An example of what AI adoption looks like in a small business: an assistant that monitors incoming email for the messages that need a response, drafts the reply through a guided workflow, and sends it in three clicks. A person approves every send.</p>
          <p><a href="mailto:lee@studiobdy.com?subject=AI%20in%20my%20business" style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px">Ask how this would work for your business</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="panel" aria-label="Illustration of the email assistant">
          <div class="row">
            <p class="meta">Watched · Acme Ltd</p>
            <p class="status">Reply needed</p>
          </div>
          <p class="title">Re: Q4 invoice query — Hannah, Acme Ltd</p>
          <div class="draft">
            <p class="label">Draft reply</p>
            <p class="body">Hi Hannah, thanks for flagging this. The October invoice was issued against the revised PO, so the difference is the agreed uplift. I've attached the breakdown…</p>
          </div>
          <div class="clicks" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="click">1 · Review</span>
            <span class="click">2 · Approve</span>
            <span class="click click-primary">3 · Send</span>
          </div>
          <p class="meta">Three clicks. Nothing leaves without a person saying so.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="steps">
        <div class="stack gap-s">
          <svg aria-hidden="true" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2"></rect><path d="M3 9l9 6 9-6"></path></svg>
          <h3 style="font-size: 18px">1 · Monitor</h3>
          <p>The senders and threads that matter are watched. Everything else is left alone.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stack gap-s">
          <svg aria-hidden="true" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 20h9"></path><path d="M16.5 3.5a2.1 2.1 0 0 1 3 3L7 19l-4 1 1-4Z"></path></svg>
          <h3 style="font-size: 18px">2 · Draft</h3>
          <p>A guided workflow turns the thread into a reply that is ready to send, in your words.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="stack gap-s">
          <svg aria-hidden="true" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 2 11 13"></path><path d="M22 2 15 22l-4-9-9-4Z"></path></svg>
          <h3 style="font-size: 18px">3 · Send</h3>
          <p>Three clicks, and a human in the loop every single time.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div class="stack gap-m">
        <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
        <h2>Studio BDY</h2>
        <img class="headshot" src="/images/lee-brady.jpg" width="640" height="640" alt="Lee Brady" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div class="stack gap-m">
        <p style="font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6">Studio BDY Ltd is the company of Lee Brady, a programme director and delivery manager based in Bath. More than 25 years of delivery in telecoms, pharma and the public sector, from running transformation programmes for major UK operators to on-site delivery for networks across Europe, plus freelance Excel and automation work for clients in many industries and several countries.</p>
        <p class="muted" style="font-size: 17px">Studio BDY delivers remotely and on site in the UK, typically engaged by a director or programme sponsor who needs an experienced hand, or by a small-business owner who wants the practical benefits of AI without the hype.</p>
        <div class="btn-row" style="font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; gap: 20px">
          <a href="/about/" style="text-decoration: none">More about Studio BDY →</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lee-brady/" rel="me noopener" style="text-decoration: none">Lee on LinkedIn ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight surface">
    <div class="container grid" style="--col: 320px; gap: 40px">
      <blockquote class="quote" style="margin: 0">
        <p>“Lee is a truly great professional. As a client of Lee's, I was always impressed with how he went above and beyond to solve problems and see deliveries to the end. Lee is a considered problem solver and he always creates options that are helpful and well thought through.”</p>
        <cite>Philip Black, CEO and Co-founder, Cormirus · client</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <blockquote class="quote" style="margin: 0">
        <p>“Lee's positive attitude, depth of knowledge and calm demeanour were significant in generating customer confidence to undertake the program and complimentary to his outstanding leadership of a multi-geography agile delivery team.”</p>
        <cite>Mark Harris MBA, senior leader on a Tier 1 telecoms transformation programme</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="panel-cta">
        <h2 style="font-size: 36px">Need delivery support?</h2>
        <p class="muted measure" style="font-size: 17px">Email lee@studiobdy.com or connect on LinkedIn. Studio BDY works remotely with clients in the UK and internationally.</p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a href="mailto:lee@studiobdy.com" class="btn btn-primary">Email lee@studiobdy.com</a>
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lee-brady/" rel="me noopener" class="btn btn-secondary">LinkedIn ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
